1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,070
Your support inbox. Every single day.

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:12,950
More humans means more cost. A generic chatbot is cheaper — until it approves a refund your policy never allowed.

3
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:24,490
This is the E-commerce Support and Returns Copilot. AI agents that resolve tickets — under your rules.

4
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:26,870
Follow one ticket.

5
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:36,590
Every message is screened first. Twenty-two attack techniques are blocked before any AI runs.

6
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:43,940
A supervisor agent sends it to specialists: orders, policy, refunds, shipping, escalation.

7
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:49,400
The order is checked against the store's records — never guessed.

8
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:57,050
Then plain code applies your return policy. Same input, same decision — every time.

9
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:05,530
Two hundred forty dollars is over the seventy-five-dollar cap. No agent can approve it. The database itself refuses.

10
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:12,490
It waits for a person — policy check and drafted reply, side by side. One click.

11
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:17,220
The AI writes the words. It never decides the money.

12
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:24,280
Thirty-six test tickets. It got every decision right. One bare prompt? Eleven percent.

13
00:01:24,930 --> 00:01:31,820
Measured cost: less than a tenth of a cent per ticket. Four in five resolved without a human.

14
00:01:32,470 --> 00:01:39,050
And it's a real product: support console, approval queue, live performance and cost.

15
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:46,240
Your policy. Your limits. Your brand. Your data. Adapted to your store.

